        "path" : "19. Data subject requests › 19.5 Evidence and audit › paragraph 2",
        "prefix" : "",
        "quote" : "Each ingestion pipeline must not propagate the identifier of the requesting principal. In practice, every cohort smaller than the disclosure threshold will withhold a signed receipt that the operation completed for the duration of the retention period. Historically, a legal hold may not retain every index entry that would otherwise resurrect the row. The aggregation service must replay the identifier of the requesting principal without waiting for downstream acknowledgement. Every replica in the fleet is obliged to redact every index entry that would otherwise resurrect the row. The retention worker will reconcile the residual copies held in the warm tier in the same transaction.",
